spans.s:
सम्-अव-√ रुध् P. -रुणद्धि (ep. also -रुन्धति), to shut up, enclose, confine, MBh. :
Pass. -रुध्यते, to be enclosed or contained in (loc.), PañcavBr.;
to be shut out of, be deprived of Hariv.

सम्-अव-√ लोक् P. -लोकयति, to look at or about, R.;
to inspect survey, ib.; Hit. (v.l.);
to behold, perceive, R.; Śak.; Kathās.

सम्-अव-√ सृज् P. -सृजति, to let go, cast or hurl down upon (loc.), MBh.;
to abandon, ib.;
to leave out, AitBr.;
to impose (a burden) upon (loc.), MBh.

(-अव-√ ईक्ष्) Ā. -अवेक्षते (ep. also P., ˚ति), to look at, behold, observe, perceive, notice, MBh.; R.;
to reflect or ponder on, consider, mind, heed, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to acknowledge, think fit or necessary, R. :
Caus. -अवेक्षयति, to cause to look at or consider, Kauś.

सम्-आ-√ 5. वस् P. -वसति, to dwell or settle in, inhabit (acc.), R.; Kām.; BhP.;
to halt, encamp (for the night), Kathās. :
Caus. -वासयति, to pitch a camp, halt, settle down, Hit.

सम्-आ-√ विश् P. -विशति, to enter together or at once, enter into, enter thoroughly, take possession of, occupy, penetrate, fill, MBh.; Hariv.; Pur.;
to sit or settle down in or on (acc. or loc.), Mn.; MBh.; R.;
to go or fall into any state or condition (acc.), MBh.;
to apply one's self to, begin, undertake, R. :
Caus. -वेशयति, to cause to enter together or thoroughly, introduce, insert, Kauś.;
to cause to sit down, Rājat.;
to conduct, lead or bring to or into (acc.), BhP.;
to place or fix (eyes or mind) upon, direct towards (loc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
 (with स्वस्मिन्) to insert in one's self, contain, Pāṇ. v, 1, 52, Sch.;
 (Ā.) to deliver over, consign or commit or entrust to (loc.), ib.

सम्-आ-√ वृ P. Ā. -वृणोति, -वृणुते, to cover all over, conceal, veil, envelop, encompass, surround, MBh.; R. &c.;
to fill, pervade, MBh.;
to obstruct, hinder, stop, ib.

सम्-आ-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, to turn back, come back, return, RV. &c. &c.;
to return home (said esp. of a Brahma-cārin or young Brāhman student of the Veda who has returned home after completing his studies in the house of a preceptor), GṛŚrS.; MBh. &c.;
to come near, approach, MBh. to turn towards (acc.; प्रदक्षिणम्, ‘with one's right side’), R.;
to turn out well, succeed, MBh. xii, 5155;
to come to nought, perish, VS. (Mahīdh.) :
Caus. -वर्तयति, to cause to return, drive away or home, RV.;
to dismiss (a pupil after the completion of his studies), ChUp.;
to repeat, recite, VarYogay.; Hcar.
